From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:08:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb+LibWebCommon+LibWebView: Add an origin access
 allowlist

An embedder may now let an origin of its own fetch from some others as
if they were the same origin: with no CORS, and with the credentials of
a same-origin request. Blink and WebKit keep the same kind of allowlist
for browser extensions, whose pages and workers reach the hosts their
users granted them this way.

Each entry is a source origin and a destination scheme and host, on any
port, with or without the host's subdomains; an empty host is any host.
Main fetch treats a request whose origin and current URL match an entry
as same-origin, so its response tainting stays "basic". A redirect to a
destination outside the list falls back to CORS, as a same-origin
request redirected to another origin does.

The UI process keeps the list
(Application::set_origin_access_allow_list) and gives it to every
WebContent and WebWorker process as it starts, and again whenever it
changes.
